      "added": 1793729827000,
      "packageName": "com.prempoddar.tune",
      "lastUpdated": 1793729827000,
      "localized": {
        "en-US": {
          "description": "<p><b>A per-app volume mixer for Android. No root.</b></p>\n<p>Turn YouTube up and Spotify down, and Tune remembers. Switch apps and each one comes back at its own level. Put a podcast on over quiet background music and both play at once, each at the volume you gave it, separately for the speaker, your headphones and every Bluetooth device.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Per-app levels</b> for media, ring, notification and alarm volume.</li>\n<li><b>Real mixing:</b> music players that share their audio play side by side at different levels.</li>\n<li><b>Learns as you go:</b> whatever volume you leave an app at becomes its level.</li>\n<li><b>Per output:</b> separate levels for the speaker, wired headphones and each Bluetooth device.</li>\n<li><b>Pin</b> an app at fixed levels.</li>\n<li><b>Volume panel</b> that moves the app you're using.</li>\n<li><b>Quick Settings tile and widget.</b></li>\n<li><b>Appearance:</b> light, dark, dusk or OLED black, Material You, fonts, shapes and haptics.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tune uses an accessibility service to see which app is in front. With Shizuku running, it can set every app's level exactly; without it, it mixes where apps allow and switches the media volume otherwise.</p>\n",
          "featureGraphic": "featureGraphic_3XYRwZbGuC4FNcGH-HcyWEPmu72ad_EYlNmOsuyKEBk=.png",
          "icon": "icon_dTW63f12DwbYsmEZKqX5c_pkbr48xdqLvzPuqK_gap4=.png",
          "name": "Tune",
          "phoneScreenshots": [
            "1.png",
            "2.png",
            "3.png",
            "4.png"
          ],
          "summary": "Per-app volume mixer: each app plays at its own level. No root",
          "whatsNew": "\u2022 Built reproducibly, so the F-Droid and GitHub versions are the same app with the same signature, and you can update from either.\n"
        }
      }
    }
